@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-inspectors`
IMPORT `g7-fourth-schedule`

-- STATUS, added by the fleet lead on 2026-10-14 (the comments below were written by the independent author and describe the state when it wrote them):
-- these 2 assertions FAILED against the modules as first written (D1: G5's s.30(b) decision never read the employee field; D2: G7's tolerant
-- designation carried an unsubstituted placeholder). Both were repaired and both now PASS, so this file is a regression test:
-- check.sh expects 0 failures here.

-- ind-b-tests-disagree.l4: assertions that FAIL and that I believe are the ENCODING's fault.
-- Each is from work/ind-b/expectations.md (scenario id given) unless marked "decided after opening".
-- They are meant to fail.  Expected: 2 assertions failed.

§ `ind-b: disagreements with the encoding`

-- D1 (I30-2).  s.30(a) has the Minister authorise inspectors "from among the employees of the Ministry", and s.2
-- defines an inspector as an employee of the Ministry whom the Minister authorised:
-- src:248 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} השר יסמיך, מקרב עובדי המשרד, מפקחים שיהיו נתונות להם הסמכויות לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן א|סימן זה}}, כולן או חלקן, לשם פיקוח על ביצוע ההוראות לפי חוק זה.
-- src:49 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”מפקח“ – עובד המשרד שהשר הסמיכו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 30|סעיף 30(א)}};
-- The exported decision `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` ("Whether the Minister may
-- authorise this Ministry employee as an inspector") carries the field `an employee of the Ministry` and never
-- reads it: a candidate who is not a Ministry employee, and meets (b)(1) to (3), is answered TRUE.  Expected: FALSE.
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` (`Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` WITH `an employee of the Ministry` IS FALSE, `record of offences` IS (`Record of offences` WITH `convicted of a criminal offence` IS FALSE, `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS FALSE, `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS FALSE, `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS FALSE), `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` IS FALSE, `received the training the Minister directed in the field of the powers he will hold` IS TRUE, `meets the further conditions of eligibility, if the Minister directed any` IS NOTHING)

-- D2 (decided after opening the encoding, from the function's own description).  The fork function
-- `the designation with direction marks and a leading R removed, in upper case` says it removes U+200E and U+200F,
-- "written by a character escape in the build".  Its second REPLACE still carries the unsubstituted placeholder
-- "{{MARK2}}", so a designation carrying a right-to-left mark (U+200F) is not recognised by the tolerant reading.
-- Expected: TRUE for 290 preceded by U+200F.  The positive controls below (R-290, 1234YF, U+200E then 290) are TRUE.
#ASSERT `the designation, read tolerantly, is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "‏290"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b control: R-290 read tolerantly` MEANS `the designation, read tolerantly, is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "R-290"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b control: 1234YF read tolerantly` MEANS `the designation, read tolerantly, is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "1234YF"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b control: U+200E then 290 read tolerantly` MEANS `the designation, read tolerantly, is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "‎290"
#EVAL `ind-b control: R-290 read tolerantly`
#EVAL `ind-b control: 1234YF read tolerantly`
#EVAL `ind-b control: U+200E then 290 read tolerantly`
